\fs36 \cf4 Major Changes
\fs28 \cf0 \
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
Double precision variables in CMFGEN are now specified in as REAL(KIND=LDP) where the kind variable is set in cur_cmf/tools/set_kind_module.f.\
The allows CMFGEN to be compiled us INTEL 80 bit arithmetic which can be useful in some SN models with molecules. On INTEL machines\
the code will run slower when this option is on. In principal, CMFGEN could also be run using 128 precision, but this will be very slow as such an\
extension is usually implemented via software. For both these case, the supplied blas and lpack routines need to be used (i.e., not those\
supplied by the INTEL math libraries).\
\
A initialization issued was fixed which occasionally caused CMF_FLUX to require way too much memory.\
\
Handling of photoionization to excited levels was changed. This affects cases where lower levels belong to the same term are not in a\
single level, and when the densities are low. Primarily effects nebular epoch supernovae models.\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\qc\partightenfactor0
