\fs36 \cf4 CMFGEN changes
\fs28 \cf0  	This is just a brief summary of some of the changes that may have a more direct\
	affect on users. \
 \
	Automatic means of adding additional species and ionization stages.\
	Requires \cf8 RVTJ, EDDFACTOR,\cf0  and \cf8 EDDFACTOR_INFO\cf0  files from exiting model.\
\
	New routines for SN gamma-ray transport.\
	Method for adding shock power (SN)\
	\
	ABS_MEAN and PLANCK_MEAN output to \cf5 RVTJ. As a consequence the new RVTJ file cannot\
	be read by older versions of CMFGEN. Future changes to RVTJ should not have this\
	effect. Older versions could be updated by implementing calls to $cmfdist/tools/rd_rvtj_v5.f\cf0 \
\
	H- ionization now referred to as H0 (not HM1) \'97 done to facilitate adding molecules.\
	\
	New routines are now utilized to compute quadrature designed  to compute moments of\
	the radiation field. This was done to overcome an accuracy issue when R(nmax) >>> R*.\
	Also affects \cf4 cmf_flux.exe\cf0 . Should be transparent to users, but this was a late change\
	to nearly a dozen routines in the current release.\
\
\
\

\fs36 CMFGEN options
\fs28 \
\
More details on these options will be provided in the CMFGEN documentation.\
     For associated keyword, look at \cf4 $cmfdist/new_main/mod_sums/rd_control_variables.f\cf0 \
\
     [CHK_NG]	Add to the VADAT file (in NG section) and set to F(alse)\
	Still working on a robust procedure to switch this option on.\
\
     [DC_METH]	Used when reading departure coefficients from an old model.\
	New option TR added, and is now the preferred option.\
                        	Gives better estimates due to changes in T at a given depth.\
\
     [PNT_SRCE]	Allow point source to be added (limited applications).\
     [TEFF_PNT_SRCE]     \
\
     [INC_SHOCK_POWER] 	For SN models (& several associated keywords)\
\
     [RD_NT-THERM_SPEC] 	Reads in non-thermal electron spectrum.\
	Set to T(rue) when debugging code. As a consequence,  the\
	non-thermal spectrum will not be recomputed every time you restart the code. \
\
    [CHK_J] 	Options designed to improve stability of radiation transfer. Can use defaults.\
    [CHK_H]\
    [CHK_XM]\
\
    [AUTO_ADD]              	Allows new DC files to be created for species without XzV_IN files. Requires \cf8 RVTJ, \
	EDDFACTOR,\cf0  and \cf8 EDDFACTOR_INFO\cf0  files from existing model, and should be\
	used with the FIXED_J=T(rue) option in VADAT. Note: Initially the changes can be huge\
	and quite a few iterations may be needed before convergence is achieved.\
\
    [AUTO_SMOOTH]	Automatically smooths populations as we iterate (primally of use when adding species\
		and ionization stages). Set to T(rue) for stellar work, may need to be F(alse) for SN work,\
		especially shell models. Note: You can use\cf4  plt_scr.exe \cf0 to fudge individual populations in \
		a CMFGEN model (you need to halt the model, use \cf4 plt_scr.exe,\cf0  and then restart). This can 	          be necessary since occasionally a few populations will go to ridiculously small values.\
\
   [USE_EHB]	Use electron heating/cooling balance as T constraint (set to F)\
   [COMP_EHB]	Compute electron heating/cooling balance as T constraint check (default is [USE_EHB]\
\
