\fs36 \cf4 GRAMON/PGPLT package
\fs28 \cf0 	A lot of new options, which can be listed using the 'H' option in the plot package.\
	Read documentation and/or \cf4 $cmfdist/pgplt/pgplot.f \cf0 to see all options. Some major\
	changes are 'CEW' and 'FEW'. The former allows line EWs to be measured using \
	cursors. The latter can use the bounds defined by CEW to measure EWs in a large 	set of model spectra (together with a box file). There is a similar (modifed) Gaussian \
	fitting option - CGF and FGF.\
\
	Options were added to the \cf4 dp_curve (curve.f) \cf0 routine to pass  curve labels directly to pgplot.\
	Call \cf4 dp_curve_lab.f.\cf0  The calls have been implemented in some options in some routines.\
\
	Options related to line ids (RID and REW) have been improved. RID reads line IDs from a\
	file created by \cf4 dispgen.exe\cf0 , and is most useful for photospheric lines.\
	REW is the EW_DATA file created by \cf4 cmf_flux.exe,\cf0  and is most useful for emission line stars	(i.e., WR stars and LBVs). Line IDs are now modified so that Sk2 becomes Si II.\
\

